    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d387">

                <pb facs="0380" n="372" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg372"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.48/256: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Then in France, to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">St.
                                Jean de Luz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-09-30T13:00:00+01:00">September 30, 1938—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 30—9:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>536. My telegram number 534, September 28, 1 p.m.<anchor n="49" xml:id="d387-f1"
                    /> Viscount Mamblas<anchor n="50" xml:id="d387-f2"/> telephoned me last night
                    that Burgos will cooperate with <pb facs="0381" n="373" xml:id="pg373"/> Friends
                    Committee on the Red Cross flour and is very appreciative of the offer. Letter
                    probably will reach me in a day or so from Burgos but with Mamblas’ assurance
                    the Red Cross may proceed as planned.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
